[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Press {lb} and {rb} together to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; turn it around the rim to keep turning. The gyro aims up, down and finely.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of it. Double tap {start} to quick save (F5) and hold it to quick load (F9).
{south} uses: doors, mounted guns, levers. {east} jumps, {west} reloads and {north} switches to the next weapon; {up} goes back to the previous one. A light push of the left stick {ls} walks quietly, and {l3} toggles crouch.
{lt} is the secondary attack: a rifle butt or pistol whip with most weapons, and the scope on a sniper rifle, which it puts up and takes down again. {rb} picks the grenade; throw it with {rt}.
Hold {lb} for the weapon ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}: pistol, rifle, submachine gun, machine gun, grenade, heavy weapon, binoculars and holster. {r3} brings out the binoculars or your papers, and {down} holsters the weapon.
{left} and {right} lean. In the base game leaning works only in multiplayer; Spearhead and Breakthrough lean everywhere.
{select} (Tab) shows the objectives, or the scores in multiplayer. Multiplayer chat needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west} and press T (all) or Y (team).
OpenMoHAA, the open-source engine for the game, uses its own executable names; add a rule for it on the Details tab to use this setup there.
These are the game's default keys from community lists and memory, not checked in the game (walk, quick save and quick load, and the leans, which are Spearhead's Z and C, especially). Compare them with Options → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The game isn't on Steam; the executable names are remembered from the GOG War Chest install and not checked. The gyro's real-world turn assumes the id Tech 3 turn of 0.022 degrees a count and a mouse sensitivity of 5, worked out, not measured; set the full turn to 16364 divided by your sensitivity.'''

